forge_moss/native/qwen35.py is ported from ComfyUI's Qwen3.5 text encoder
(https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI, commit a09d037, comfy/text_encoders/qwen35.py, GNU General Public
License v3.0), with the numerics of transformers' Qwen3.5 model (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers,
commit 09281b8, src/transformers/models/qwen3_5/modeling_qwen3_5.py), Copyright The HuggingFace Team and The
Qwen Team, Apache License 2.0. tests/reference/qwen35_hf.py is a transcription of that transformers file without
the transformers framework, used only by the tests.

forge_moss/native/text_engine.py follows MOSS-Image's reference pipeline
(https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT, pipeline_moss_image.py), Copyright OpenMOSS Team,
Apache License 2.0.

forge_moss/native/huggingface/moss-image/tokenizer/tokenizer.json is the Qwen3.5 tokenizer as MOSS-Image ships it
(https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT), Qwen Team, Apache License 2.0. text_encoder/config.json and
transformer/config.json restate the MOSS-Image configurations; vae/config.json is the FLUX.2 autoencoder
configuration as Forge Neo ships it.

The MOSS-Image weights are not part of this extension. They are released by the OpenMOSS Team under the Apache
License 2.0 (https://huggingface.co/OpenMOSS-Team/MOSS-Image-SFT, https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image).

forge_moss/native/spectrum.py independently adapts the Chebyshev/ridge forecasting
idea of Spectrum (Han et al., https://github.com/hanjq17/Spectrum, MIT-licensed
reference implementation). It forecasts MOSS velocities rather than copying the
upstream feature forecaster. No upstream Spectrum source is bundled.

The preceding statement applies only to spectrum.py (Balanced mode).
forge_moss/native/spectrum_policy.py now extracts the predictor, branch state,
configuration and adaptive/manual scheduling from Rkkss/ComfyUI-Spectrum-MOSS
nodes.py, revision 3fde0674b29342565e7f42a0674af48d65aabc4a, Copyright Rkkss
and contributors, GPL-3.0-only (LICENSE-SPECTRUM). That source credits Han et al.'s
Spectrum method and awdqwdasdg's GPL Comfyui-Spectrum-Qwen2.1 implementation.
spectrum_hidden.py provides the separate native Forge lifecycle/head adapter.
The extension's combined distribution remains AGPL-3.0; preserved GPL notices
and corresponding vendored source are included.

